              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_KwEnHH": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Everyday steps.</strong> Many women get real relief from simple changes:</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_NGe8XV": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<ul><li>Keep a consistent bedtime and wake time, and keep the bedroom cool, dark and quiet.</li><li>Cut back on caffeine after midday and alcohol in the evening. Both fragment sleep, even if alcohol helps you drift off.</li><li>If you cannot sleep, get up and do something calm in low light until you feel sleepy. Cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia (CBT-I) is a well-proven approach.</li></ul>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": true,
                "line_height": 36,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 0,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_mAtczE": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Products that may help.</strong> Some women find hormone-free supplements helpful, though the evidence is mixed and quality varies. We stock a small selection chosen for manufacturing quality, and we show the evidence level on every product page. Supplements are not FDA-approved to treat any condition, and what works for one woman may do nothing for another.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
                "line_height": 26,
                "line_height_mobile": 24,
                "custom_spacing": true,
                "margin_top": 0,
                "margin_bottom": 20,
                "margin_left": 0,
                "margin_right": 0
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "text_wejyc7": {
              "type": "text",
              "settings": {
                "text": "<p><strong>When to see a clinician.</strong> If poor sleep lasts more than a few weeks and affects your days, or a partner notices loud snoring, gasping or pauses in your breathing, see a clinician. Treating night sweats, checking for sleep apnea and accessing CBT-I can all help. Bacton does not prescribe; we can help you prepare for that conversation.</p>",
                "text_style": "body",
                "alignment": "left",
                "text_color": "",
                "custom_font_size": false,
                "font_size": 16,
                "font_size_mobile": 15,
                "custom_line_height": false,
